# LearningBot console environment.
#
# Every variable below is read by code in this repository, and every variable
# the code requires is below. If you add one here, name its reader; if a reader
# disappears, delete the variable. An environment file that documents variables
# nothing reads, and omits the ones the code requires, is worse than no file.
#
# Never put a secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* value: those are inlined into the
# browser bundle.

NODE_ENV=production

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED - Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/supabase/config.ts, and every route and page through it.
# Missing: the console cannot reach the database at all. Sign-in, the
# workspace, the conversation and every admin surface fail immediately.
#
# The publishable key is intentionally browser-safe: it stays constrained by
# the signed-in user's JWT plus row level security. Never substitute a secret
# or service-role key here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_replace_me

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED - OpenAI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/provider-runtime.ts (answers and question classification)
# and the three routes under src/app/api/learning/voice/.
# Missing: every answer fails with `provider_not_configured` and all three
# voice routes return 503. Authoring, analytics and administration still work.
#
# This key is live spend. Every provider call is metered into
# public.cost_ledger, and a per-tenant budget is enforced in SQL before the
# call is made. Set a client's budget with
# `platform_admin_set_tenant_cost_policy` before onboarding them, and watch
# spend with `platform_admin_cost_overview`.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED - conversation operation secret
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/app/api/learning/respond/route.ts.
# Missing, shorter than 32 characters, or not matching a currently valid
# database row: the assistant cannot read the tenant persona and cannot record
# an assistant message, so chat stops working. Nothing else is affected.
#
# This is a shared secret between this deployment and the database. The plain
# value lives ONLY here. The database stores its SHA-256 digest in
# app_private.learning_operation_secrets for capability
# `conversation.answer.record`, and that row carries a mandatory expiry.
#
# 32 to 512 characters from [A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]. Generate with:
#     openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\n' | tr '+/' '-_'
#
# PROVISIONING (once, before the first client):
#   1. Generate the value and set it in the deployment's environment.
#   2. Signed in as a platform administrator, run:
#        select public.platform_admin_register_operation_secret(
#          'conversation.answer.record',
#          '<the generated value>',
#          90,                     -- days of validity, 1..365
#          'vercel-production'     -- label: where the plaintext lives
#        );
#   3. Confirm with:
#        select public.platform_admin_operation_secret_status();
#      It reports validSecretCount and daysRemaining per capability, and never
#      a token.
#
# ROTATION (no downtime - the verifier accepts ANY currently valid secret, so
# the outgoing and incoming secrets overlap):
#   1. Generate a NEW value.
#   2. Register it:
#        select public.platform_admin_register_operation_secret(
#          'conversation.answer.record', '<new value>', 90, 'vercel-production'
#        );
#      Both secrets are now valid. Nothing is interrupted.
#   3. Replace this variable with the new value and redeploy. Verify chat.
#   4. Revoke the old one:
#        select public.platform_admin_revoke_operation_secret(
#          '<old secretId>', 'rotation completed'
#        );
#      The RPC refuses to revoke the last valid secret unless you pass
#      allow_last => true, so step 2 cannot be skipped by accident.
#
# EXPIRY: `platform_admin_operation_secret_status()` reports days remaining,
# and `platform_admin_cost_overview()` embeds it. Rotate below 14 days.
LEARNINGBOT_CONVERSATION_OPERATION_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - embedding worker operation secret
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: POST /api/learning/embeddings. The route refuses every request
# unless this is at least 32 characters, and the caller must present the same
# value as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` or `x-learningbot-operation-token`.
# Its digest must also exist as a valid `knowledge.embedding.worker` row in
# app_private.learning_operation_secrets - this variable alone grants nothing.
#
# Missing: no answers are lost. Published courses are retrievable lexically the
# moment they are published; embeddings only improve ranking.
#
# Provision and rotate it exactly like the conversation secret above, passing
# the capability 'knowledge.embedding.worker' instead.
# LEARNINGBOT_EMBEDDING_OPERATION_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - telemetry outbox drain operation secret
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: POST /api/ops/telemetry-outbox/drain. The route refuses every
# request unless this is at least 32 characters, and the caller must present
# the same value as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` or
# `x-learningbot-operation-token`. Its digest must also exist as a valid
# `telemetry.outbox.drain` row in app_private.learning_operation_secrets -
# this variable alone grants nothing.
#
# Missing: no data is lost. public.telemetry_outbox already writes durably on
# every usage event; without this configured, rows simply accumulate
# unclaimed instead of being drained and eventually purged. Call the route on
# a schedule (Vercel Cron, a GitHub Action, or any authenticated caller - no
# cron dependency is baked into the route itself) once this is set.
#
# Provision and rotate it exactly like the conversation secret above, passing
# the capability 'telemetry.outbox.drain' instead. The retry budget, claim
# lease, backoff and retention window are configured separately, in SQL, via
# `platform_admin_set_telemetry_outbox_policy`.
# LEARNINGBOT_TELEMETRY_OUTBOX_OPERATION_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - model selection
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/learning-provider.ts (answers) and
# src/lib/question-classification.ts (labels).
# Missing: the defaults shown below are used.
# LEARNINGBOT_LLM_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# LEARNINGBOT_CLASSIFIER_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - price book
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/cost-metering.ts.
# Missing: built-in estimates are used. They are deliberately conservative - an
# unrecognised model is priced high, so spend is overstated rather than hidden.
# Set this to the figures on your own provider invoice; every budget decision
# is only as good as these numbers.
#
# Amounts are micro units: millionths of one major currency unit, so 1250000
# is $1.25. Text models price input and output separately per million tokens;
# audio models price one billed unit (a second, a character, a session).
# LEARNINGBOT_MODEL_PRICES={"gpt-5.6-luna":{"inputPerMillionTokens":1250000,"outputPerMillionTokens":10000000},"gpt-4o-mini-tts":{"perUnit":15}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - character avatars (PLAN.md Section 7.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/app/api/agent/avatar/route.ts.
# Uses the same OPENAI_API_KEY above (required); no separate credential.
#
# Missing: character avatar generation returns `provider_not_configured` and
# the Studio panel shows a clear "not configured" state. Nothing else is
# affected — a missing, absent or unconfigured avatar never blocks chat, and
# the monogram fallback (brandInitial() in components/app-shell/brand.ts)
# renders exactly as it does today.
#
# The OpenAI model used to generate each of the five poses.
# LEARNINGBOT_AVATAR_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1
#
# Micro-USD (millionths of one US dollar, same unit cost-metering.ts uses)
# charged per generated pose image, five poses per set. This route cannot add
# a shared LEARNINGBOT_MODEL_PRICES entry for this model without editing
# src/lib/cost-metering.ts, which another phase of work owns concurrently, so
# it keeps its own small, overridable estimate instead - deliberately a
# plausible overstatement rather than an understatement, same philosophy as
# cost-metering.ts's UNKNOWN_MODEL_PRICE. Defaults to 70000 (=$0.07/image).
# LEARNINGBOT_AVATAR_IMAGE_PRICE_MICRO=70000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - Stripe billing (PLAN.md Section 10)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/billing/stripe.ts, and every route under
# src/app/api/billing/. Every Stripe call in this codebase is hosted
# Checkout, the hosted Billing Portal, or a server-to-server API/webhook call
# — nothing here ever accepts, logs or stores a card number, CVC or expiry.
#
# Missing any of the three required values below: readBillingConfig()
# returns null and every route that touches Stripe returns a clear
# `stripe_not_configured` (503) instead of throwing. The margin policy form,
# the manual subscription override and the rest of the platform billing
# panel keep working with Stripe fully unconfigured — comping or correcting
# an account must never depend on Stripe being reachable.
#
# The Secret Key. Live spend authority once configured; never exposed to the
# browser (this is a server-only variable, not NEXT_PUBLIC_*).
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# The signing secret for the webhook endpoint below (Stripe Dashboard ->
# Developers -> Webhooks -> your endpoint -> "Signing secret"). Verified by
# hand in src/lib/billing/stripe.ts (HMAC-SHA256 over the raw request body,
# Stripe's own construction) rather than the `stripe` SDK, so this repository
# adds no new dependency for it. An unsigned or forged webhook is rejected
# before its Stripe event id is even read (PLAN.md S10.3).
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# The Stripe Price id for metered usage billing, attached as a second
# subscription item on every Checkout Session this platform creates. Usage
# reporting assumes this price is configured at $0.01 per unit — the worker
# reports quantity in whole minor currency units (cents); see the comment on
# app_private.billing_micro_to_minor in the billing migration.
STRIPE_METERED_PRICE_ID=

# One Stripe Price id per flat subscription plan. A plan with no price
# configured here cannot be checked out — `checkout.create` returns
# `plan_not_configured` — but its section entitlements and manual overrides
# still work.
# STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=
# STRIPE_PRICE_GROWTH=
# STRIPE_PRICE_ENTERPRISE=
#
# PROVISIONING the two operation secrets below (once, before enabling
# billing) — same mechanism and same rotation procedure as
# LEARNINGBOT_CONVERSATION_OPERATION_TOKEN above, with these capabilities:
#   select public.platform_admin_register_operation_secret(
#     'billing.stripe.webhook', '<generated value>', 90, 'vercel-production'
#   );
#   select public.platform_admin_register_operation_secret(
#     'billing.operations', '<generated value>', 90, 'vercel-production'
#   );

# Read by: POST /api/billing/webhook. Authorizes `billing_webhook_ingest`
# after the Stripe signature above has already verified — defense in depth,
# the same two-layer pattern the embedding worker and telemetry drain use.
# Missing: the route returns `worker_not_configured` (503) rather than
# accepting an unauthenticated write. Stripe retries, so no delivery is lost.
# LEARNINGBOT_BILLING_WEBHOOK_OPERATION_TOKEN=

# Read by: POST /api/billing/usage-report and POST
# /api/billing/dunning-sweep. Call these on a schedule (Vercel Cron, a
# GitHub Action): usage-report reports metered `cost_ledger` rows to Stripe
# (idempotent — each row is committed to public.billing_usage_reports at
# most once, ever); dunning-sweep advances a tenant from a payment-failure
# grace period to the "sections dark" stage once that window elapses.
# Missing: no usage is ever billed and no account ever moves past its grace
# period automatically — a platform administrator can still bill or dun by
# hand from the platform panel. Nothing here can cut off an active
# conversation; billing failure never stops learning.
# LEARNINGBOT_BILLING_OPERATIONS_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Removed 2026-07-26. These had no reader anywhere in the repository, and their
# presence here implied capabilities that do not ship:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY_VAULT_REF, PROVIDER_CREDENTIAL_VAULT_REF,
#   OIDC_ISSUER_URL, OIDC_CLIENT_ID, OIDC_JWKS_URL,
#   OIDC_ALLOWED_ALGORITHMS, OIDC_MAX_TOKEN_AGE_SECONDS,
#   OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_VAULT_REF, DATABASE_URL,
#   LEARNINGBOT_FIXTURE_PREVIEW, LEARNINGBOT_FIXTURE_PREVIEW_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT,
#   LEARNINGBOT_FIXTURE_PREVIEW_AUTHORIZATION, LEARNINGBOT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN
# Re-add any of them only together with the code that reads it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
